Inspect Application Observability services on this Grafana stack.

Commands: list finds services across Knowledge Graph scopes; get reports one service's RED metrics and topology; operations lists one service's native operations; dependencies reports its upstream callers or downstream services; quality reports instrumentation checks; runtime reports JVM or Node.js runtime metrics. Service inventory, identity, topology, quality, and runtime metadata require an active Knowledge Graph and Application Observability integration. Native operation metrics come from the configured Prometheus datasource and do not require Knowledge Graph. The optional namespace for native operations is a Prometheus job prefix, which may differ from a Knowledge Graph namespace. Results include links into the app.

```ts
mcp__Grafana_Cloud__app_observability_handler(args: {
// list (every service) | get (RED KPIs for one service) | operations (RED KPIs per operation under one service) | dependencies (services upstream/downstream of one service) | quality (Knowledge Graph instrumentation-quality report for one service) | runtime (JVM/Node.js runtime metrics for one service)
command: "list" | "get" | "operations" | "dependencies" | "quality" | "runtime",
// Pin the Prometheus datasource holding the App O11y metrics, when the tool reports several candidates
datasourceUid?: string,
// For dependencies: upstream (callers of the service) or downstream (services it calls). Defaults to downstream.
direction?: "upstream" | "downstream",
// Knowledge Graph environment scope for list, get, dependencies, quality, or runtime. For runtime it selects service metadata but does not filter native metrics.
env?: string,
// For list, operations, and dependencies: cap rows after sorting, up to 50.
limit?: integer, // maximum: 50, exclusiveMinimum: 0
// For list, get, dependencies, quality, and runtime: Knowledge Graph Service namespace scope, which need not equal the Kubernetes namespace, OTel service.namespace, or native job prefix. For operations: prefix of the native Prometheus job label (<namespace>/<service>).
namespace?: string,
// Service name (required for get, operations, dependencies, quality, runtime; from the list command)
service?: string,
// Knowledge Graph site scope for list, get, dependencies, quality, or runtime. For runtime it selects service metadata but does not filter native metrics.
site?: string,
// For list, operations, and dependencies: sort rows by request rate, error ratio, p95 latency, or name. Unset preserves the default order.
sortBy?: "rate" | "errors" | "p95" | "name",
// Sort direction for sortBy. Defaults to desc for RED metrics and asc for name.
sortDirection?: "asc" | "desc",
}): Promise<unknown>;
```

Inspect Application Observability operations on this Grafana stack.

Commands: top ranks operations across services by latency, errors, or request rate; get reports full RED metrics, including p99 latency, for one service and operationName. Both commands read native Prometheus span metrics independently of Knowledge Graph. The optional namespace is the native Prometheus job prefix, which may differ from a Knowledge Graph namespace. Results include links into the app.

```ts
mcp__Grafana_Cloud__app_observability_operation_handler(args: {
// top (slowest/highest-error/busiest operations across every service, unscoped to any one service) | get (full RED KPIs, including p99, for one already-identified operation under one service)
command: "top" | "get",
// Pin the Prometheus datasource holding the App O11y metrics, when the tool reports several candidates
datasourceUid?: string,
// For top: cap the number of rows returned, applied after sorting. Defaults to 10 — this is a small triage view of the worst offenders, not a full inventory dump. Maximum 50.
limit?: integer, // maximum: 50, exclusiveMinimum: 0
// Native Prometheus job prefix, not Knowledge Graph scope. For top: match jobs beginning <namespace>/; for get: select job <namespace>/<service>. It may differ from Kubernetes or OTel service namespace.
namespace?: string,
// Legacy direct-tool input for the operation/span name.
operation?: string,
// Required for get: the exact operation/span name to look up.
operationName?: string,
// Required for get: the service the operation belongs to.
service?: string,
// For top: sort by request rate, error ratio, or p95 latency. Defaults to p95 (slowest first).
sortBy?: "rate" | "errors" | "p95",
// For top: sort direction. Defaults to desc (worst/busiest first).
sortDirection?: "asc" | "desc",
}): Promise<unknown>;
```

Send a message to Grafana Assistant and wait for the full text reply. The assistant may use tools, metrics, logs, and other stack context—broader than firing one isolated data-source query.

Use for open-ended questions, triage, or anything that needs assistant reasoning and tool use, in addition to the more targeted MCP tools.

**Multi-turn:** pass contextId from a previous ask_assistant result to continue the same conversation.

**Time:** complex tasks can take several minutes; the call blocks until the reply is done or the request times out. Consider running this tool as a background task if able.

```ts
mcp__Grafana_Cloud__ask_assistant(args: {
// Optional. Context ID from a previous ask_assistant response to continue the same conversation.
contextId?: string,
// The question or instruction to send to Grafana Assistant (natural language).
prompt: string,
}): Promise<unknown>;
```

Historical/indexed memory search across your Grafana stack: infrastructure/service groups, dashboards, past investigations, mostly-resolved IRM incidents, and alert-rule definitions.

Covers architecture, topology, dashboard discovery (including panel queries), alerts by meaning or content, past incidents, past investigations/RCAs, and broad "what do we know about X?" questions. Investigation and incident searches default to records created in the last three calendar months.

Results are indexed snapshots, not live telemetry, and can be stale or incomplete: an infrastructure result's dependency list comes from a sample of recent traces and can miss calls. Live metrics, logs, traces, alert state, and on-call or incident data are not searched.

Returns results grouped by collection with titles, summaries, links, and metadata (including datasource UIDs for infrastructure results).

```ts
mcp__Grafana_Cloud__assistant_search(args: {
// Required, non-empty set of collections to search; there is no search-all value. dashboards: dashboards and their panel queries. alertRules: alert rule definitions. incidents: past incidents. investigations: past investigations and RCAs. infrastructure: indexed architecture, topology, and stored datasource mappings. Listing all five includes infrastructure.
collections: Array<"dashboards" | "investigations" | "incidents" | "alertRules" | "infrastructure">,
// Exclusive investigation and incident creation-time upper bound (RFC3339). Must be after startTime when both are supplied.
endTime?: string,
// Optional positive integer retrieval limits keyed by dashboards, infrastructure, investigations, incidents, or alertRules. Omitted entries keep existing defaults (20 dashboards, 3 infrastructure, 5 investigations, 5 incidents; alert rules use their retrieval limit). Limits are passed to collection retrieval backends, with no post-retrieval truncation. Filtering and deduplication may return fewer matches.
limits?: {
// Maximum alert-rule results, from 1 to 200. Omit to retain the existing retrieval limit of 20 alert rules.
alertRules?: integer,
// Maximum dashboard results, from 1 to 200. Omit to retain 20 dashboards.
dashboards?: integer,
// Maximum incident results, from 1 to 200. Omit to retain 5 incidents.
incidents?: integer,
// Maximum infrastructure results, from 1 to 200. Omit to retain 3 infrastructure memories.
infrastructure?: integer,
// Maximum investigation results, from 1 to 200. Omit to retain 5 investigations.
investigations?: integer,
},
// A natural-language search query describing what to find across infrastructure/service groups, dashboards, past investigations, incidents, and alert rules. Service names, error messages, and symptoms improve results.
query: string,
// Inclusive investigation and incident creation-time lower bound (RFC3339). Defaults to the start of the last three calendar months.
startTime?: string,
}): Promise<unknown>;
```

