Tell the Hatchable team about a problem with the Hatchable platform itself (a footgun, friction point, or surprising behavior) that you hit during this build. Each report is stored in Hatchable's own feedback queue, where the Hatchable team reviews it; it is not sent to any other service.

**When to call:** any time a platform constraint, undocumented limit, misleading error, missing helper, or stale doc cost you more than ~5 minutes to figure out — OR any time you successfully reach for a non-obvious workaround that future builds shouldn't have to rediscover. Calling mid-build (right after the workaround) is more useful than at the end of the build, because the painful details are still fresh.

**Report quality matters:** the title should be one sentence ("TextDecoder caps decoded strings at 32 KB per decode() call"). The body should describe what you tried, the error you got, and the workaround. Write for the Hatchable engineer who will fix it, not for yourself.

**What a report contains:** only the fields you fill in below. Describe the platform behavior; do not include the user's personal data, secrets or credentials, or their app's private content.

**Don't use this for:** generic praise, app-level bugs in the user's own code, anything that's already documented (search skills first via list_skills).

```ts
